# Phase 6.3-5 Closure Megaudit — IDE-AWARE OPUS lane

Engine: /Users/sanzhar/Documents/Sanzhar/Sanzhar/quantlab/quantlab-quantbook/quantbook-engine @ feat/quantbook-engine 9429ac48193
IDE:    /Users/sanzhar/Documents/Sanzhar/Sanzhar/quantlab/quantlab/extensions/quantlab @ feat/visualise-v1 cb3ca7cedca

## VERDICT: SHIP

The IDE consumer side is consistent with the Phase 6.3 EngineSession binding contract that is
about to freeze. The headline cross-repo risk (error-code allowlist parity) is CLEAN by the
strongest available test: the IDE `KNOWN_QUANTBOOK_ERROR_CODE_RECORD` (session.ts) and the
`QuantbookErrorCode` union (types.ts) are an EXACT set match modulo the single intentional
`'unknown'` fallback (record == union − {unknown}, verified programmatically — 63 record keys,
64 union members). Every engine-emittable code reaches a known IDE entry; no engine code buckets
to 'unknown'; the only IDE entries the engine never emits are the two the IDE is contractually
responsible for producing locally. All 28 napi `#[napi(object)]` DTOs have IDE interface mirrors.
All 47 `Session` napi methods have an IDE `SessionInstance` signature and a loader presence-block
entry. The wire contract (native-first dual-read + `[code]` prefix fallback + schemaVersion assert
on both snapshot + delta) is correctly implemented. No HIGH findings.

NOTE ON METHOD: an earlier draft of this lane was built on a WRONG error-source path
(`crates/ql-exec/src/session/error.rs`, which does not exist) and a wrong 18-code inventory. That
draft was DISCARDED. This verdict rests on the REAL `EngineError` at
`crates/ql-session/src/error.rs` and on programmatic set-diffs run with python against the actual
files (not the redaction-prone shell grep counts).

