## 1. ERROR-CODE ALLOWLIST PARITY (the headline check) — CLEAN

### Method
Parsed the IDE `KNOWN_QUANTBOOK_ERROR_CODE_RECORD` keys (session.ts:775-894) and the
`QuantbookErrorCode` union members (types.ts:2207+) programmatically, then cross-checked each
record code against whole-tree `grep -rl --include=*.rs "\"<code>\"" crates` (excluding target).

### Record vs Union — EXACT
- record keys: 63
- union members: 64 (the 63 + `'unknown'`)
- `record === union − {'unknown'}`: **TRUE** (zero asymmetry).
This is exactly the compile-enforced `Record<Exclude<QuantbookErrorCode,'unknown'>, true>`
invariant doing its job. A code added to the union without a record key (or vice versa) would
fail TS compile; the runtime check confirms the two are in lockstep at this HEAD.

### Engine-emittable codes → all known to IDE
Every code in the IDE record resolves to an engine emission site. Grouped by source:

EngineError named constructors / map_runtime_err / map_oplog_err / operation / dto
(crates/ql-session/{error.rs,lib.rs,dto.rs,operation.rs}, crates/ql-exec/src/session.rs):
  formula_parse, formula_bind, bad_cell, sheet_not_found, sheet_name_duplicate, bad_sheet_name,
  too_many_sheets, sheet_not_deleted, invalid_chunk_rows, unknown_format_id,
  format_counter_exhausted, recompute_iteration_cap, conflicting_ops, conflicting_batch_ops,
  name_reserved, table_create_rejected, table_not_found, table_column_not_found,
  table_column_rejected, table_resize_rejected, transaction_not_found, transaction_id_exhausted,
  operation_not_found, invalid_version_token, invalid_version_vector, unsupported_schema_version,
  oplog_serialize, oplog_deserialize, oplog_schema, oplog_loro, undo_manager_failed,
  replay_failed, canceled, panic, invalid_state, session_busy, not_implemented_in_v1_core,
  unmapped_oplog_error.
map_xlsx_err / map_csv_err (crates/ql-exec/src/session.rs, ql-io):
  xlsx_io, xlsx_zip, xlsx_calamine, xlsx_xml_parse, xlsx_malformed_ooxml, xlsx_unsupported_feature,
  xlsx_export, xlsx_engine, csv_io, csv_parse, csv_exceeds_limits, csv_sheet_not_found,
  unmapped_xlsx_error, unmapped_csv_error.
map_function_registry_err (crates/ql-functions/src/registry.rs): function_exists, function_not_found.
bad_argument: the FFI-boundary validators (`bad_argument_error`, `validate_u32/u16_index`) in
  crates/ql-bindings-node/src/lib.rs — `ErrorClass::BadArgument => "bad_argument"` at lib.rs:4299.
COLLAB layer codes (ql-collab / ql-collab-ws, reached via collab_session_error_to_napi /
  transport_error_to_napi / websocket_error_to_napi — these ride the SAME `[code]` prefix the IDE
  parses, and the IDE wires the live grid through CollabSession today): transport_io,
  transport_closed, websocket_invalid_url, websocket_connect_failed, websocket_handshake_failed,
  websocket_runtime_error, session_oplog, session_presence, session_undo, session_replay.
PERSISTENCE codes (persistence_error_to_napi, crates/ql-bindings-node/src/lib.rs:537-544):
  qbook_error, session_oplog (shared), qbook_unsupported_version, qbook_truncated_header,
  qbook_unknown (the `#[non_exhaustive]` catch-all the mapper itself can emit — a REAL engine
  emission, correctly in the allowlist).
unmapped_persistence_error: the No-Fallbacks loud-Internal catch-all in the owning-layer
  persistence mapper.

### IDE-known but engine-never-emits (the only two — both correct by design)
- `unsupported_schema_version`: emitted BOTH by the engine (ql-session/src/error.rs + lib.rs +
  ql-io/src/qbook_format.rs) AND produced by the IDE's `assertSupportedSchemaVersion`
  (session.ts:951). Dual-producer — correct: the IDE is the snapshot/delta-ingest producer per
  contract §4.1, the engine is the qbook/op-wire producer.
- `unknown`: the parser fallback sentinel, intentionally excluded from the record (Exclude<>) and
  present only in the union + ALL_QUANTBOOK_ERROR_CODES. Correct (V2.7 Opus MEDIUM-1 invariant).

### Per-cell DIAGNOSTIC codes (udf_*) — correctly EXCLUDED
The 8 `udf_*` codes appear 0× in EngineError (error.rs) — they are NOT thrown errors. They live
on the SEPARATE diagnostic channel: `DiagnosticJson.code` (8 `udf_*` references in types.ts, in
the QuantbookDiagnostic/Diagnostic DTO, not the error union). The session.ts comment at :818-819
explicitly documents this exclusion. Correct.

### CODE-DIFF TABLE (set difference both ways)
| Direction                                   | Result |
|---------------------------------------------|--------|
| engine-emittable codes NOT in IDE record    | NONE   |
| IDE record codes NOT emitted anywhere in engine | NONE (every record key has an emission site; `worker_untrusted_workspace` is the lone IDE-thrown one — see below) |
| IDE record − IDE union                       | ∅      |
| IDE union − IDE record − {unknown}           | ∅      |
| udf_* diagnostics in error union             | NONE (correctly on DiagnosticJson.code instead) |

### One IDE-thrown code worth a confirming note (not a defect)
`worker_untrusted_workspace` is in the record but appears 0× in `crates/**.rs`. It is thrown by
the IDE itself (`injectUdfWorker`, workspace-trust gate) per the session.ts:803-804 comment — an
IDE-side producer, exactly like `unsupported_schema_version`. Confirmed IDE-only via grep of both
trees. Correct by design.

