## 3. SessionInstance METHOD SIGNATURES — CLEAN
Brace-matched the engine `impl Session { … }` block and the IDE `interface SessionInstance { … }`,
then diffed the method-name sets:
- engine-bound (47 methods) NOT in IDE SessionInstance: NONE.
- IDE SessionInstance sigs NOT bound on the engine Session: NONE.
Exact one-to-one. Spans the full 6.3 surface: addSheet, setValue, setFormula, clear, recalcDirty,
recalcAll, startRecalcDirty, startRecalcAll, awaitRecalc, cancel, operationStatus, snapshot, cell,
listSheets, lifecycleState, validateFormula, queryRange, markVolatilesDirty, setFormat,
registerFormat, close, open, save, import, export, renameSheet, deleteSheet, restoreSheet,
moveSheet, setName, createTable, renameTable, renameColumn, resizeTable, dropTable, batch,
beginTransaction, txnAdd, commitTransaction, rollbackTransaction, writeRange, publishDataset,
bindRange, refreshSource, materializeQuery, registerFunction, unregisterFunction, listFunctions,
setUdfWorker, pollEvents, snapshotDelta, undo, redo, canUndo, canRedo.
The loader (loader.ts:328-437) carries a presence-block entry for every one of these (6.1B inc.2d
through 6.3-3 + the X1/X2 parity backfill for close/registerFunction/unregisterFunction/listFunctions),
so a stale cdylib fails at the boundary, not at a use site. The `__forcePanicForTest` method is
test-only and correctly absent from the IDE sig + loader.

