## 4. WIRE CONTRACT — CLEAN
- `parseQuantbookError` (session.ts:1008) does native-first dual-read: reads the thrown JS Error's
  own-property `.code` FIRST (set by `throw_structured` via Env::create_error + Object::set at
  lib.rs:4275-4299, returning Status::PendingException), validating it through `isQuantbookErrorCode`;
  then reads `.class`/`.details`/`.retryable`. Falls through to the `[code]`-prefix cause-chain walk
  (regex `/^\[([a-z][a-z0-9_]*)\]\s*(.*)$/s`, session.ts:919) for the FFI `bad_argument` validators
  + collab/persistence/udf-spawn errors (which keep the `[code]` prefix string and a generic napi
  `.code` like 'GenericFailure' that the allowlist guard rejects). Dual-format, monotonic. Matches
  the engine's two emission shapes exactly (structured throw for EngineSession results; `[code]`
  prefix for `bad_argument`/collab/persistence/udf).
- `EngineError::Display` `[code] message` (engine) ↔ IDE bracket regex: the regex anchors `^\[code\]`
  and the engine prefix format is `[{code}] {message}` — match. The `details` JSON-string carry
  (napi serde-json feature off) is read as `typeof === 'string' ? : undefined` (session.ts:1040) —
  faithful to the current engine behavior (native nested-object details is filed-forward).
- `assertSupportedSchemaVersion` (session.ts:951) is the sole IDE producer of
  `unsupported_schema_version`; it is invoked on BOTH snapshot and delta ingest (schemaVersion is
  declared on both DTOs; cellGridLogic.ts also calls it). The engine's own qbook/op-wire
  `unsupported_schema_version` is a distinct, separately-emitted instance of the same code — not
  conflated. QUANTBOOK_SCHEMA_VERSION = 1 (session.ts:937) matches engine ql_session::SCHEMA_VERSION
  = 1 (the u16=1 constant; the u32=2/u32=8 SCHEMA_VERSION constants are the ql-oplog op-wire and
  qbook-envelope versions, a DIFFERENT axis, not the DTO contract version).

