## FINDINGS
INFO · ide:src/quantbook/types.ts:2207 + session.ts:775 · The error-code surface is a SUPERSET of
  the v1 product EngineError taxonomy because it ALSO carries the collab-layer codes (transport_*,
  websocket_*, session_presence/undo/replay) and persistence codes that ride the legacy
  CollabSession `[code]` path the live grid still uses. This is correct for TODAY (the IDE consumes
  both surfaces) but means "frozen contract" for 6.3 ≠ "this exact union". When CollabSession is
  re-founded on WorkbookSession (decision-lock §1 D1), revisit whether the collab codes should
  remain in the same union or split. Not blocking the 6.3 freeze.
INFO · engine:docs/api/session-api.md:484 + crates/ql-bindings-node/src/lib.rs:4242 · `bad_argument`
  is the binding's OWN FFI-validation code (uniform class=BadArgument, no details), kept on the
  `[code]`-prefix string path, NOT a structured EngineError thrown by the owning layer. The IDE
  reads it via the prefix branch. Consistent on both sides; noted because the brief framed
  `bad_argument` as an "FFI bad_argument path" — confirmed it exists exactly as described.
LOW · ide:src/quantbook/types.ts (FormatIdJson) · Engine `builtin`/`customCounter` are `Option<f64>`
  (6.3-2 H1 no-coercion hardening) but the TS mirror types them `number?`. Semantically fine (wire
  value is a whole u32; both sides treat it as a JS number), but the TS type does not encode the
  "integer-domain" constraint. Cosmetic; the engine validator (`validate_u32_index` via
  `session_format_id_from_json`) is the enforcement point. Not blocking.

## VERIFIED CLEAN
- record == union − {unknown} (63 == 63), compile-enforced + runtime-confirmed.
- Every engine-emittable code (EngineError + collab + persistence + registry + bad_argument) is in
  the IDE allowlist; NONE buckets to 'unknown'.
- Only IDE-known-not-engine-emitted entries are the two intentional IDE producers
  (unsupported_schema_version dual-producer, worker_untrusted_workspace) + the unknown fallback.
- 8 udf_* per-cell diagnostics correctly on DiagnosticJson.code, absent from the thrown-error union.
- All 28 napi DTOs have IDE interface mirrors; field names/optionality/Buffer/BigInt consistent;
  schemaVersion on both snapshot + delta; CellValue.blank on both; fullRebuildReason 4-member union
  matches full_rebuild_reason_str.
- All 47 Session napi methods have an IDE SessionInstance sig AND a loader presence-block entry;
  zero orphans either direction; __forcePanicForTest correctly excluded.
- parseQuantbookError native-first dual-read covers structured throw + [code]-prefix; regex matches
  EngineError::Display form.
- assertSupportedSchemaVersion is the snapshot+delta-ingest producer of unsupported_schema_version;
  QUANTBOOK_SCHEMA_VERSION (1) == engine ql_session::SCHEMA_VERSION (1).
